<title>CHINA: China bank to extend $720 mln in mortgage loans.</title>
<headline>China bank to extend $720 mln in mortgage loans.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run China Construction Bank plans to extend mortgage loans totalling six billion yuan ($720 million) to home buyers this year, the China Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank would extend mortgage loans to buyers of apartments built with public housing funds, bank vice-president Shi Chungui said. The loans would mature in a maximum of 20 years.</p>
<p>The bank accounts for 60 percent of the total mortgage loans extended by Chinese banks, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>By the end of 1996, the bank had extended $20 billion in mortgage loans to over one million home buyers, it said.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
